CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ default-constructed unique_ptr is null: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[unique.ptr.single.ctor]/1 -- a default-constructed unique_ptr is null.  Fixed
by modelling C++17 inheriting constructors ([class.inhctor.init]): a base
default constructor inherited via using Base::Base makes the derived class
(here libstdc++'s __uniq_ptr_data, which only declares defaulted move members)
default-constructible, synthesized as the defaulted default constructor it is
exactly equivalent to.  Previously the constructor chain silently failed and
the stored pointer stayed nondet.
